From 8a79b99944e9f666b07f6c2a4b137c6378fd6d9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mossa <cgmossa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 19:20:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make rust-analyzer compile for wasm32-unknown-unknown

The native build is unaffected. Two target-specific changes are needed
to get the workspace through `cargo check`/`cargo build`:

- `home` (transitively pulled in via `toolchain`) only supports Unix and
  Windows. Move it under a `cfg(not(wasm32-unknown-unknown))` target
  table and have `get_cargo_home()` return `None` on wasm.
- `url::Url::{from_file_path, to_file_path}` are unavailable on
  `wasm32-unknown-unknown`. Add a small `WasmFileUrlExt` trait in
  `crates/rust-analyzer/src/lsp/wasm_file_url.rs` that provides a
  faithful `file://` encoder/decoder for the wasm target, and import
  it at the existing call sites under the same `cfg`.

This produces a working `target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/
librust_analyzer.rlib`, which is what the .rust-analyzer-wasm demo
links against.

AI-assisted: drafted with Claude (Anthropic) and reviewed by hand;
disclosed per CONTRIBUTING.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
